// D1568 — a bare `null` DELIVERED at every position, against a plain nullable-STRUCT type,
// with no scenery at all. `emitObjField` seeds `pendingStructIdx` from `sFieldTgtStructIdx`
// for a code-15 (nested-struct / nullable-struct) field, so `{ f: null }` lowers; the
// field-WRITE arm of `emitAssign` — the other half of every field code — never seeded it, so
// `w.f = null` reached `emitNullLitNode` with every seed unset and refused loudly on a
// `vl check`-clean program.
//
// The point of the template is that it carries NO union arm and NO second global: D1563's
// matrix reached this position too, but through a leaked variant seed, and the two must be
// separable. This one is red at `struct_field_assign` alone.
//
// The un-annotated face of a position that pins nothing is EXPECTED to refuse: a bare `null`
// with nothing typing it has no rep to take, which is the language's answer, not a gap.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type C = { a: i32, b: i32 }
// @@VALUE@@
null
// @@TYPE@@
C | null
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v.a)
// @@MISS@@
print("none")
// @@WANT@@
none
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: a map whose VALUE is `null` cannot be told from a missing key — the read's `!= null` guard is false either way, so the proof prints nothing at both seeds
